RUNG 0 — pile: cat for piles
  Every other rung starts here. Read lines from the files named (or stdin), merge them,
  keep each line once, and write the pile back out. Output is a pile, so rungs chain.

  usage:  0-pile FILE.eoe ...        or      ... | 0-pile

read pile:
    texts  = contents of each .eoe file named, or stdin if none
    lines  = for each text: parse each row as [left, right]    (report rows that aren't)
    lines  = union of all lines, sorted, duplicates removed
    lines  = drop lines whose ids collide                      (report them)
    return lines, and an index: by id, by left end, by right end

words given    = arguments that are neither files nor --flags
help if asked  = on --help, or too few words: print this file's header and stop

main:
    write each line of (read pile) as [left, right]
